# A single triangle. The smallest valid OBJ, used by the loader fixture tests.
#
# Layout: three vertices, one normal, one UV, one face. The face line uses the
# `v/vt/vn` reference form so a parser has to handle all three reference kinds.
#
# Exported from Blender as "Wavefront (.obj)" with "Write Normals" and
# "Write UVs" enabled, triangulated.

# 3 vertex positions
v 0.000000 0.000000 0.000000
v 1.000000 0.000000 0.000000
v 0.000000 1.000000 0.000000

# 1 vertex normal, pointing at +Z
vn 0.000000 0.000000 1.000000

# 3 UV coordinates
vt 0.000000 0.000000
vt 1.000000 0.000000
vt 0.000000 1.000000

# 1 triangle: position/uv/normal indices, 1-based
f 1/1/1 2/2/1 3/3/1
